#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## Eigencube: a Rubik's cube solved by linear algebra, a port of Steffen
## Smolka's eigencube.py (github.com/smolkaj/eigencube, MIT). Each of
## the 26 cubelets is the integer point c of {-1, 0, 1}^3 where it sits
## in the solved cube and carries a rotation matrix R: it sits now at
## R c. A quarter turn of the face with outward normal v moves the
## cubelets with v . (R c) > 0 by one matrix product. The model and the
## solver are the Eigencube library of X_eTaL-libraries (pinned in
## LIBRARIES_COMMIT, read from work/libraries by "just libraries"); this
## program scrambles a cube and solves it with it.

"ec:" u_se< "Eigencube"

### A scramble

# 20 random moves ("just run eigencube" draws a new one each time; the
# tests run "xetal run --seed 1"), in the usual notation.
sc := r_oll! 20 r_eshape 12
"scramble: " c_at ec:n_ame sc
x := sc ec:d_o ec:solved
# Its stickers, a face per row (U D F B R L), each cell the face its
# color belongs on: 1 to 6, white, yellow, green, blue, red, orange.
ec:s_tickers x

### Solved

(sol, lens, e) := 1 ec:s_olve x
"solution: " c_at ec:n_ame sol
"moves: " c_at f_ormat t_ally sol
# The moves each stage took: the top layer a cubelet at a time
# (stages 1 to 9), the middle layer (10 to 17), the bottom edges (18
# to 25) and the bottom corners' places (26 to 29), then the
# endgame's corner twists.
lens c_at e
# After the solution: every face one color.
ec:s_tickers sol ec:d_o x
"solved: " c_at f_ormat ec:s_olved? sol ec:d_o x
